# DRAFT -- NOT A TASK. Deliberately not named `task.yaml`: the suite loader
# (harness/v2sbench/tasks.py, load_suite) only picks up directories that
# contain `task.yaml`, so this file is inert and `v2sbench tasks --tier
# t4-game` does not list it.
#
# It is committed so the rung's shape is on record. Three things must exist
# before it becomes a task, and none of them is a formality:
#
#   1. oracle/  -- a scripted policy that reaches the milestone from the
#      provisioned seed, in a fresh container. This is the blocker.
#   2. A milestone threshold chosen against a MEASURED reference policy,
#      the way env/2048/calibrate.py bands and env/crafter/calibrate.py
#      random set theirs. The numbers below are a guess and are marked so.
#   3. A frozen, hashed interface (env/nethack/PROTOCOL.draft.md is a
#      draft) and a checker that replays the journal rather than trusting
#      a reported outcome.
schema_version: 1
id: nethack-dlvl4-xp3
tier: t4-game
title: "DRAFT: survive to dungeon level 4 at experience level 3 (NetHack)"
goal: >-
  A NetHack game is already running in this directory, played through the
  `v2s-game` command. Play it. When you stop, the character must be alive,
  standing on dungeon level 4 or deeper, and at experience level 3 or
  higher, within the 5000-turn budget. `v2s-game help` states the
  interface and the key vocabulary.
discoverability: poor
feedback_bandwidth: silent
knowledge_gap:
  summary: >-
    PLACEHOLDER. The intended gap is the one BALROG documented as the
    knowing-doing gap: a model can state NetHack facts correctly in a quiz
    and then eat rotten food, pray at the wrong time, or melee a floating
    eye. The procedural version -- eat before Weak becomes Fainting, do
    not melee a blue `e`, keep Elbereth for emergencies, descend rather
    than grind -- is what a tutorial video teaches and what a skill should
    carry. It must be written against one specific, probe-able fact rather
    than this list.
  probe_question: >-
    PLACEHOLDER.
  probe_answer_pattern: 'PLACEHOLDER'
  taught_at: [0.0]
environment:
  image: v2sbench/t4-game-nethack:0.1
  workdir: /work
  network: none
  seedable: true
  setup:
    - install -m 0755 v2s-game /usr/local/bin/v2s-game && rm -f v2s-game
    # NetHackScore-v0, not NetHackChallenge-v0: the Challenge task refuses
    # to be seeded (see env/nethack/README.md).
    - V2S_GAME_PROVISION=1 v2s-game init --seed 20481 --turns 5000 >/dev/null
budget:
  max_turns: 80
  wall_secs: 2400
  max_usd: 4.0
check:
  entrypoint: check.py          # does not exist yet
  required_assertions:
    - journal-present
    - game-as-provisioned
    - keys-replay
    - journal-is-consistent
    - alive-at-dlvl4-xp3
  score:
    metric: >-
      BALROG's NetHack progress metric (dungeon level x experience level
      mapped to empirical human win probability from a human-gameplay
      dataset), recomputed by the checker from its own replay. MIT,
      vendored from github.com/balrog-ai/BALROG at a pinned commit --
      NOT from PyPI, where the name belongs to an unrelated library.
    milestones:
      - dlvl-2
      - dlvl-3
      - dlvl-4
      - xp-2
      - xp-3
      - alive-at-dlvl4-xp3
      - reached-minetown
oracle:
  entrypoint: solve.sh          # DOES NOT EXIST -- this is why it is a draft
  modality: shell
video:
  tier: hermetic
  ref: nethack-dlvl4-xp3        # no recipe written; a NetHack recipe needs
  sha256: null                  # width 1920 / height 1080 for 80 columns
license: >-
  NetHack is distributed under the NetHack General Public Licence and the
  NetHack Learning Environment under its own licence; both are free and
  neither needs a purchase or a ROM. Nothing is committed here. An image
  that is published carries the NGPL source-availability obligation.
attribution: >-
  NetHack Learning Environment, Kuettler et al. 2020 (arXiv:2006.13760).
  Progress metric and the knowing-doing gap: BALROG, arXiv:2411.13543
  (MIT).
notes: >-
  EXPECTED BAND IS A GUESS, NOT A MEASUREMENT. Full-game LLM progress on
  NetHack is 1.5-13%, a floor effect, which is why the task is bounded at
  all; dungeon level 4 with experience level 3 inside 5000 turns is
  proposed because it is reachable by ordinary early-game play and not by
  flailing, but until a reference policy has been measured on the
  provisioned seed that is an assertion rather than a band. Do not run
  this task against any arm before that measurement exists.
